IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2003 (NSW) -- the operative Act, from the seat of the principal: the person who gives the
-- power of attorney (s 3(1) "principal ... means the person giving the power").
--
-- SEAT: the principal. Every exported question is one the principal would ask: "Is my power enduring?", "Is it
-- irrevocable?", "Can my attorney act for me once I cannot understand?", "Can my attorney give my money away, or use it
-- for themselves?", "Can my substitute act now?", "Does my power end if one attorney dies?", "Is it suspended because my
-- estate is managed?", "Can I ask the tribunal to review it?". A second seat, the principal's family member, named
-- beneficiary or other interested person, is in poa-seat-family.l4. The attorney gets no seat of their own here (the
-- attorney's duties, s 49, are encoded as what they mean for the principal). The Supreme Court, the Civil and
-- Administrative Tribunal (NCAT), the Registrar-General and the NSW Trustee and Guardian get no seat.
--
-- Provisions: ss 3, 4, 5 (definitions); s 6 (which instruments the Act governs); ss 8-13 and Schedule 3 (prescribed
-- powers: trustee functions, gifts, benefits); ss 15, 16 (irrevocable powers); ss 17, 18 (initial and supervening
-- incapacity); ss 19, 20, 21 (enduring powers); s 25 (interstate enduring powers); ss 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 35
-- (review: which tribunal, termination and confirmation orders, who may apply); s 36(5) (no revocation while declared
-- incapable); s 44 (certified copies); ss 45, 45A (delegation and substitutes); ss 46-50 (termination and suspension);
-- s 52 (registration for deeds affecting land). Others are in comments or out: see NOTES.md.
--
-- ASSUMED THROUGHOUT (fork F1): unless a question asks otherwise, the power was created by an instrument executed on or
-- after this Act commenced (s 6(1)); an older power is governed by the continued Conveyancing Act 1919 provisions
-- (Schedule 1, out of scope) except for s 25, Part 5 and Part 6 Division 3 (s 6(5)).
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "only if", "unless" or "where", a period the text fixes, a flat "does not" or "cannot"),
-- or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given (the general law, kept by s 7, or the instrument decides);
-- each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 2 March 2025; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Powers of Attorney Act 2003`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 6: which provisions govern the power.
DECLARE `The law that governs my power of attorney` IS ONE OF
    `this Act`
    `the continued Conveyancing Act 1919 provisions in Schedule 1, with s 25, Part 5 and Part 6 Division 3 of this Act`

-- s 19(2) "prescribed witness means" (a)-(e). The Minister's approved course (para (c)) and the regulations (para (e))
-- are not deposited: whether a course was completed, or a person is prescribed, is asked.
DECLARE `The person who witnessed my signature` IS ONE OF
    `a registrar of the Local Court`
    `an Australian legal practitioner`
    `a licensed conveyancer who has completed the Minister's approved course`
    `an employee of the NSW Trustee and Guardian who has completed the Minister's approved course`
    `an employee of a trustee company who has completed the Minister's approved course`
    `a licensed conveyancer, or such an employee, who has not completed the approved course`
    `a legal practitioner qualified overseas, instructed and employed independently of any lawyer I appointed as attorney`
    `a legal practitioner qualified overseas, not so independent`
    `a person the regulations prescribe as a witness`
    `another person`

-- s 3(1) "valuable consideration includes marriage but does not include a nominal consideration, even if it has some
-- value".
DECLARE `What I received for giving the power` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `only a nominal consideration`
    `marriage`
    `money, property or another real benefit`

-- s 16(1) (a)-(f), from the seat of an individual principal (para (f), a corporation's dissolution, is not asked).
DECLARE `What has happened` IS ONE OF
    `I did something about the power without my attorney's agreement`
    `I became bankrupt`
    `I lost mental capacity`
    `I became a mentally incapacitated person`
    `I became a managed missing person`
    `I died`
    `something else`

-- Schedule 3 cl 1(2)(a)(i), (3): relative and close friend of a principal.
DECLARE `Who would receive the gift` IS ONE OF
    `my mother, father, spouse, child, stepchild, brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister or grandchild`
    `such a relative of my registered or domestic-relationship partner`
    `a close friend of mine`
    `someone else`

-- ss 12, 13 and Schedule 3 cls 2, 3: who would get the benefit.
DECLARE `Who would benefit` IS ONE OF
    `my attorney`
    `a third party named in my instrument's Schedule 3 expression`
    `a third party not named in it`

-- Schedule 3 cls 2(2)(a), 3(2)(a): the expenses a benefit may meet.
DECLARE `The expense the benefit would meet` IS ONE OF
    `housing`
    `food`
    `education`
    `transportation`
    `medical care and medication`
    `some other expense`

-- s 5 (a)-(g): a vacancy in the office of an attorney.
DECLARE `What has happened to my attorney` IS ONE OF
    `my appointment of them was revoked`
    `they renounced the power`
    `they died`
    `they became bankrupt`
    `they are a corporation that was dissolved`
    `they lost the capacity to continue to act as attorney`
    `a circumstance the regulations prescribe`
    `none of these`

-- s 46: how two or more attorneys were appointed.
DECLARE `How my attorneys were appointed` IS ONE OF
    `jointly`
    `severally`
    `jointly and severally`
    `I appointed only one attorney`

-- ss 26, 33: the review tribunals.
DECLARE `The review tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `the Civil and Administrative Tribunal`
    `the Supreme Court`

-- s 35(1): who is an interested person.
DECLARE `My place in relation to the power` IS ONE OF
    `I am an attorney under the power, even if my appointment was purportedly revoked`
    `I am the principal`
    `I am the principal's guardian`
    `I am the principal's enduring guardian`
    `someone else, such as a relative or friend`

-- s 44(1)(a): who certified the copy. Sch 5 cl 3 points to a class of persons in a repealed regulation (not deposited).
DECLARE `Who certified the copy` IS ONE OF
    `I did, as the principal`
    `a person of the class the regulations prescribe`
    `another person`

-- The party and act of the s 49 rule.
DECLARE `Attorney party` IS ONE OF `the attorney`
DECLARE `Attorney act` IS ONE OF `do an act under the power knowing it has ended or been suspended`

§§ `s 6 -- which law governs the power`

-- s 6(1) the Act applies to a power created by an instrument executed on or after commencement; s 6(2), (3) an older
-- power stays under Part 16 of, and Schedule 7 to, the Conveyancing Act 1919 (copied in Schedule 1); s 6(5) but s 25,
-- Part 5 and Part 6 Division 3 extend to it. The commencement day is fixed by proclamation (s 2), not deposited: asked.
@export Which law governs my power of attorney: this Act, or the old Conveyancing Act provisions (s 6)?
GIVEN `my instrument was executed before this Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed the document creating your power of attorney before the Powers of Attorney Act 2003 commenced (the day was fixed by proclamation; check it if unsure)
GIVETH A `The law that governs my power of attorney`
`Which law governs my power of attorney` MEANS
    IF `my instrument was executed before this Act commenced`
    THEN `the continued Conveyancing Act 1919 provisions in Schedule 1, with s 25, Part 5 and Part 6 Division 3 of this Act`
    ELSE `this Act`

§§ `ss 3, 4, 5 -- definitions worked out`

-- s 4(1) "a person is incommunicate if (a) the person suffers from any physical or mental incapacity (whether of a
-- temporary or permanent nature) that makes the person unable (i) to understand communications respecting the person's
-- property or affairs, or (ii) to express the person's intentions ..., or (b) the person is unable to receive
-- communications ... because the person cannot be located or contacted." s 4(2): drug- or treatment-induced counts.
GIVEN `an incapacity makes the principal unable to understand communications about their property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an incapacity makes the principal unable to express their intentions about their property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal cannot be located or contacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is incommunicate` `an incapacity makes the principal unable to understand communications about their property or affairs` `an incapacity makes the principal unable to express their intentions about their property or affairs` `the principal cannot be located or contacted` IF
       `an incapacity makes the principal unable to understand communications about their property or affairs`
    OR `an incapacity makes the principal unable to express their intentions about their property or affairs`
    OR `the principal cannot be located or contacted`

-- s 5 "there is a vacancy in the office of an attorney if" (a)-(g).
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What has happened to my attorney`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a vacancy in the office of` `what happened` IF
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(1) "valuable consideration includes marriage but does not include a nominal consideration".
GIVEN `what I received` IS A `What I received for giving the power`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is valuable consideration` `what I received` IF
    CONSIDER `what I received`
    WHEN `marriage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `money, property or another real benefit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 19 -- enduring powers of attorney`

-- s 19(2) "prescribed witness means" (a)-(e): a "means" definition, closed.
GIVEN `the witness` IS A `The person who witnessed my signature`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed witness` `the witness` IF
    CONSIDER `the witness`
    WHEN `a licensed conveyancer, or such an employee, who has not completed the approved course` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a legal practitioner qualified overseas, not so independent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another person` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 19(1) "An instrument that creates a power of attorney creates an enduring power of attorney for the purposes of this
-- Act if (a) the instrument is expressed to be given with the intention that it will continue to be effective even if
-- the principal lacks capacity through loss of mental capacity after execution of the instrument, and (b) execution of
-- the instrument by the principal is witnessed by a person who is a prescribed witness (not being an attorney under the
-- power), and (c) there is endorsed on, or annexed to, the instrument a certificate by that person stating that" (i)-(v).
@export Does my document create an enduring power of attorney, one that keeps working if I lose mental capacity (s 19)?
GIVEN `my document says it is to continue even if I lose mental capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document says it is given with the intention that it will continue to be effective even if you later lose mental capacity
      `the person who witnessed my signature` IS A `The person who witnessed my signature` @desc Who witnessed you signing. One of: "a registrar of the Local Court", "an Australian legal practitioner", "a licensed conveyancer who has completed the Minister's approved course", "an employee of the NSW Trustee and Guardian who has completed the Minister's approved course", "an employee of a trustee company who has completed the Minister's approved course", "a licensed conveyancer, or such an employee, who has not completed the approved course", "a legal practitioner qualified overseas, instructed and employed independently of any lawyer I appointed as attorney", "a legal practitioner qualified overseas, not so independent", "a person the regulations prescribe as a witness", "another person"
      `my witness is one of my attorneys` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness is also an attorney appointed under this power
      `the witness's certificate states all five matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a certificate by the witness is written on or attached to the document stating that the witness (i) explained its effect to you before you signed, (ii) you appeared to understand it, (iii) the witness is a prescribed witness, (iv) the witness is not an attorney under it, and (v) the witness saw you sign
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my document create an enduring power of attorney` MEANS
    IF     `my document says it is to continue even if I lose mental capacity`
       AND `is a prescribed witness` `the person who witnessed my signature`
       AND (NOT `my witness is one of my attorneys`)
       AND `the witness's certificate states all five matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 19(1) "if" (a), (b) and (c)

§§ `s 20 -- the attorney must accept`

-- s 20(1) "An enduring power of attorney does not operate to confer any authority on an attorney until the attorney has
-- accepted the appointment by signing the instrument creating the power." (2) only the attorneys who accept; (3) at
-- execution or any time after; (4) substitutes too. An "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE before
-- acceptance, JUST FALSE after; the answer never claims the attorney has authority.
@export Is this attorney still barred from acting under my enduring power of attorney, because they have not yet accepted by signing it (s 20)?
GIVEN `my power is an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is an enduring one (see the s 19 question)
      `this attorney has signed the document to accept the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this attorney (or substitute attorney) has signed your power of attorney document to accept the appointment, at the time you signed or later
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this attorney still barred from acting under my enduring power` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my power is an enduring power of attorney`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 20 speaks only of enduring powers; the text is silent on others)
    ELSE IF `this attorney has signed the document to accept the appointment`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 15 -- irrevocable powers of attorney`

-- s 15 "An instrument that creates a power of attorney creates an irrevocable power of attorney for the purposes of this
-- Act if (a) the instrument is expressed to be irrevocable, and (b) the instrument is given for valuable consideration or
-- is expressed to be given for valuable consideration."
@export Does my document create an irrevocable power of attorney (ss 3(1), 15)?
GIVEN `my document says it is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document says it is irrevocable
      `what I received for giving the power` IS A `What I received for giving the power` @desc What you received in return for giving the power. One of: "nothing", "only a nominal consideration" (a token amount), "marriage", "money, property or another real benefit"
      `my document says it is given for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document says it is given for valuable consideration (whatever you actually received)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my document create an irrevocable power of attorney` MEANS
    IF     `my document says it is irrevocable`
       AND (   `it is valuable consideration` `what I received for giving the power`
            OR `my document says it is given for valuable consideration`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 15 "if" (a) and (b)

§§ `s 16 -- what does not end an irrevocable power`

-- s 16(1) the power "is not revoked or otherwise terminated by, and remains effective despite, the occurrence of any of
-- the following" (a)-(f); (2) "except to the extent that the instrument ... provides otherwise". s 28: the Supreme Court
-- may still terminate it (see `Can the Supreme Court end my irrevocable power`).
@export If my power of attorney is irrevocable, does this event end it (s 16)?
GIVEN `my power is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is irrevocable (see the s 15 question)
      `what has happened` IS A `What has happened` @desc The event. One of: "I did something about the power without my attorney's agreement", "I became bankrupt", "I lost mental capacity", "I became a mentally incapacitated person", "I became a managed missing person", "I died", "something else"
      `my document provides otherwise for this event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document itself says the power ends (or is affected) on this event
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does this event end my irrevocable power` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my power is irrevocable`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 16 is silent on other powers; the general law, kept by s 7, decides)
    ELSE IF `my document provides otherwise for this event`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the Act: the instrument decides, s 16(2))
         ELSE CONSIDER `what has happened`
              WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the s 16(1) list; the text is silent)
              OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 16(1), a flat "is not revoked or otherwise terminated"

§§ `s 28 -- the Supreme Court may end an irrevocable power`

-- s 28 "The Supreme Court may order that an irrevocable power of attorney is terminated ... if the Court considers that
-- (a) the objects ... have been carried out, or (b) ... have become incapable of being carried out, or (c) the power of
-- attorney is otherwise exhausted." The Court's view is asked.
@export Can the Supreme Court order that my irrevocable power of attorney is ended (s 28)?
GIVEN `my power is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is irrevocable (see the s 15 question)
      `the Court considers the power's objects have been carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court considers that what the power was given for has been done
      `the Court considers the power's objects can no longer be carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court considers that what the power was given for can no longer be done
      `the Court considers the power is otherwise exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court considers the power otherwise used up
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Supreme Court end my irrevocable power` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my power is irrevocable`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 28 speaks only of irrevocable powers)
    ELSE IF    `the Court considers the power's objects have been carried out`
            OR `the Court considers the power's objects can no longer be carried out`
            OR `the Court considers the power is otherwise exhausted`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 28 "if the Court considers"

§§ `ss 16, 18, 21 -- when I can no longer understand`

-- s 18 "A power of attorney is effective to the extent that it concerns any act within its scope that is of such a
-- nature that is not beyond the understanding of the principal through mental incapacity at the time of the act."
-- s 21(1) an act within an enduring power "that is beyond the understanding of the principal through mental incapacity
-- at the time of the act is as effective as it would have been had the principal understood"; (3) unless a contrary
-- intention is expressed in the instrument. s 16(1)(c) an irrevocable power is not terminated by the principal's mental
-- incapacity, (2) unless the instrument provides otherwise. Where none of these saves the act, the Act does not say the
-- act is ineffective (s 18 has no "only"): NOTHING (fork F4).
@export Can my attorney still act for me, within the power, in something I cannot understand at the time because of mental incapacity (ss 16, 18, 21)?
GIVEN `I understand the nature of the act at the time it is done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time your attorney does the act, its nature is within your understanding despite any mental incapacity
      `my power is an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is an enduring one (see the s 19 question)
      `my power is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is irrevocable (see the s 15 question)
      `my document expresses a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document says it is not to continue, for this kind of act, once you lose mental capacity
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney act for me in something I cannot understand` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I understand the nature of the act at the time it is done` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 18
           IF `my document expresses a contrary intention` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (ss 16(2), 21(3): the instrument decides)
           IF `my power is an enduring power of attorney` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 21(1)
           IF `my power is irrevocable` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 16(1)(c)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 18 limits the grant "to the extent" with no "only"; the general law decides; fork F4)

§§ `ss 17, 29-32 -- a power given while I could not understand it`

-- s 17(1) a power "is not ineffective only because any act within the scope of the power is ... beyond the
-- understanding of the principal through mental incapacity at the time the power is given"; (2) "However, a power of
-- attorney does not authorise an attorney to do any such act unless it is authorised by or under this Act." s 32: an
-- act after a Supreme Court confirmation order is "as good ... as if ... the principal were of full capacity".
@export Can my attorney do an act that was beyond my understanding when I gave the power (ss 17, 32)?
GIVEN `the Supreme Court has confirmed the power for this act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has made an order under ss 29, 30 or 31 confirming the power to the extent it covers this act, and the order has taken effect
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney do an act I could not understand when I gave the power` MEANS
    IF `the Supreme Court has confirmed the power for this act`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 32
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 17(2) "does not authorise ... unless"

-- s 29: confirm "if it appears to the Court that the nature of the act was not beyond the understanding of the principal
-- ... at the time when the power was given". s 30: confirm "to the extent that it appears to the Court that (a) the
-- principal has affirmed the power ..., and (b) the principal had sufficient mental capacity to affirm". s 31(1): confirm
-- "if it appears to the Court that (a) the principal is incapable of affirming the power because (i) ... continuation of
-- mental incapacity ... or (ii) the principal is incommunicate, and (b) it is for the benefit of the principal"; (2)
-- unless a contrary intention is expressed. The Court's view is asked; the order itself is discretionary ("may").
@export Can the Supreme Court, on my application, confirm a power of attorney I gave (ss 29, 30, 31)?
GIVEN `the act was within my understanding when I gave the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Court that the nature of the act was within your understanding when you gave the power
      `I have since affirmed the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have affirmed the power, before or during the court proceedings
      `I had the mental capacity to affirm it when I did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had enough mental capacity to affirm the power when you did
      `the incapacity I had when I gave the power continues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot affirm the power because the mental incapacity you had when you gave it continues
      `an incapacity makes me unable to understand communications about my property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physical or mental incapacity (temporary or permanent, including one caused by a drug or treatment) makes you unable to understand communications about your property or affairs
      `an incapacity makes me unable to express my intentions about my property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such an incapacity makes you unable to express your intentions about your property or affairs
      `I cannot be located or contacted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot be located or contacted
      `confirming it is for my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Court that confirming the power is for your benefit
      `my document expresses a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document says it is not to be confirmed in this way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Supreme Court confirm my power of attorney` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the act was within my understanding when I gave the power` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 29
           IF `I have since affirmed the power` AND `I had the mental capacity to affirm it when I did` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 30
           IF     (   `the incapacity I had when I gave the power continues`
                   OR `the principal is incommunicate` `an incapacity makes me unable to understand communications about my property or affairs` `an incapacity makes me unable to express my intentions about my property or affairs` `I cannot be located or contacted`)
              AND `confirming it is for my benefit`
              AND (NOT `my document expresses a contrary intention`)
           THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 31
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- ss 29, 31 "if it appears to the Court"; s 30 "to the extent that"

§§ `ss 8-13, Schedule 3 -- prescribed powers: trustee functions, gifts and benefits`

-- s 8 "An instrument ... that is in or to the effect of a form prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this
-- section and is duly executed creates a prescribed power of attorney". The form is in the regulations (not deposited):
-- asked.
GIVEN `my document is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN, `my document is duly executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a prescribed power of attorney` `my document is in the prescribed form` `my document is duly executed` IF
    `my document is in the prescribed form` AND `my document is duly executed`

-- s 10 "A prescribed power of attorney does not confer authority to exercise any function as a trustee that is conferred
-- or imposed on the principal."
@export Can my attorney, under my prescribed-form power of attorney, act in my place as a trustee (s 10)?
GIVEN `my document is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is in (or to the effect of) the form prescribed by the regulations under s 8
      `my document is duly executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document was properly signed (executed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney act as trustee in my place` MEANS
    IF `it is a prescribed power of attorney` `my document is in the prescribed form` `my document is duly executed`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 10, a flat "does not confer"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 10 speaks only of prescribed powers; the general law decides others)

-- s 11(1) "A prescribed power of attorney does not authorise an attorney to give a gift of all or any property of the
-- principal to any other person unless the instrument creating the power expressly authorises the giving of the gift."
-- (2) the Schedule 3 expression authorises the gifts Schedule 3 specifies. Schedule 3 cl 1(2) "authorises an attorney to
-- give a gift only if (a) the gift is (i) to a relative or close friend of the principal, and (ii) of a seasonal nature
-- or because of a special event (including, for example, a birth or marriage), or (b) the gift is a donation of the
-- nature that the principal made when the principal had capacity or the principal might reasonably be expected to make,
-- and the gift's value is not more than what is reasonable having regard to all the circumstances and, in particular,
-- the principal's financial circumstances and the size of the principal's estate." Reasonableness is asked.
@export Can my attorney, under my prescribed-form power of attorney, give this gift of my property (s 11, Schedule 3 cl 1)?
GIVEN `my document is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is in (or to the effect of) the form prescribed by the regulations under s 8
      `my document is duly executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document was properly signed (executed)
      `my document expressly authorises this gift in its own words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document, in words other than the Schedule 3 wording, expressly authorises your attorney to give this gift
      `my document includes the Schedule 3 wording for reasonable gifts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document says "I authorise my attorney to give reasonable gifts as provided by section 11 (2) of the Powers of Attorney Act 2003"
      `who would receive the gift` IS A `Who would receive the gift` @desc Who would receive the gift. One of: "my mother, father, spouse, child, stepchild, brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister or grandchild", "such a relative of my registered or domestic-relationship partner", "a close friend of mine" (someone with a close personal relationship with you and a personal interest in your welfare), "someone else"
      `the gift is seasonal or for a special event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift is of a seasonal nature (for example a birthday or holiday gift) or because of a special event such as a birth or marriage
      `the gift is a donation of the kind I made or would be expected to make` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift is a donation of the kind you made when you had capacity, or might reasonably be expected to make
      `the gift's value is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift's value is no more than reasonable in all the circumstances, in particular your financial circumstances and the size of your estate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney give this gift of my property` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it is a prescribed power of attorney` `my document is in the prescribed form` `my document is duly executed`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 11 speaks of prescribed powers; the general law it restates decides others)
           IF `my document expressly authorises this gift in its own words` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 11(1), with s 9(1)
           IF `my document includes the Schedule 3 wording for reasonable gifts`
           THEN IF     (   (`a relative or close friend` AND `the gift is seasonal or for a special event`)
                        OR `the gift is a donation of the kind I made or would be expected to make`)
                   AND `the gift's value is reasonable`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE  -- Schedule 3 cl 1(2) "only if"
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 11(1) "does not authorise ... unless"
    WHERE
        `a relative or close friend` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who would receive the gift`
            WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 12(1) a prescribed power "does not authorise an attorney to execute an assurance or other document, or to do any
-- other act, as a result of which a benefit would be conferred on the attorney unless the instrument creating the power
-- expressly authorises the conferral of the benefit"; s 13(1) the same for a benefit on a third party. Schedule 3 cls 2(2),
-- 3(2): the expression authorises a benefit (on the attorney, or on "a named third party") "only if (a) the benefit meets
-- ... expenses ... in respect of ... (i) housing, (ii) food, (iii) education, (iv) transportation, (v) medical care and
-- medication, and (b) the benefit is not more than what is reasonable".
@export Can my attorney, under my prescribed-form power of attorney, use my property to benefit themselves or someone else (ss 12, 13, Schedule 3 cls 2, 3)?
GIVEN `my document is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is in (or to the effect of) the form prescribed by the regulations under s 8
      `my document is duly executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document was properly signed (executed)
      `who would benefit` IS A `Who would benefit` @desc Who would benefit. One of: "my attorney", "a third party named in my instrument's Schedule 3 expression", "a third party not named in it"
      `my document expressly authorises this benefit in its own words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document, in words other than the Schedule 3 wording, expressly authorises this benefit
      `my document includes the Schedule 3 wording for this kind of benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document includes the Schedule 3 wording "I authorise my attorney to confer benefits on the attorney (or on the named persons) to meet ... reasonable living and medical expenses"
      `the expense the benefit would meet` IS A `The expense the benefit would meet` @desc The expense the benefit would pay for. One of: "housing", "food", "education", "transportation", "medical care and medication", "some other expense"
      `the benefit is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the benefit is no more than reasonable in all the circumstances, in particular your financial circumstances and the size of your estate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney use my property to benefit themselves or another` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it is a prescribed power of attorney` `my document is in the prescribed form` `my document is duly executed`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (ss 12, 13 speak of prescribed powers; the general law decides others)
           IF `my document expressly authorises this benefit in its own words` THEN JUST TRUE  -- ss 12(1), 13(1)
           IF `my document includes the Schedule 3 wording for this kind of benefit`
           THEN IF `a person the wording can reach` AND `a listed expense` AND `the benefit is reasonable`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE  -- Schedule 3 cls 2(2), 3(2) "only if"
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- ss 12(1), 13(1) "does not authorise ... unless"
    WHERE
        `a person the wording can reach` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who would benefit`
            WHEN `a third party not named in it` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `a listed expense` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the expense the benefit would meet`
            WHEN `some other expense` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 5, 20(4), 45, 45A -- delegates and substitutes`

-- s 45(1) "An attorney under a power of attorney cannot appoint a substitute, delegate or sub-attorney unless the
-- instrument creating the power expressly provides for the attorney to do so." (2) "Nothing in this section enables an
-- attorney irrevocably to appoint a substitute, delegate or sub-attorney unless the instrument ... expressly provides".
@export Can my attorney appoint someone else (a substitute, delegate or sub-attorney) to act under my power of attorney (s 45)?
GIVEN `my document expressly lets my attorney appoint someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document expressly allows your attorney to appoint a substitute, delegate or sub-attorney
      `the appointment would be irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney wants to make the appointment irrevocable
      `my document expressly lets my attorney appoint someone irrevocably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document expressly allows your attorney to make such an appointment irrevocably
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney appoint someone else to act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `my document expressly lets my attorney appoint someone`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 45(1) "cannot ... unless"
           IF `the appointment would be irrevocable` AND (NOT `my document expressly lets my attorney appoint someone irrevocably`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 45(2), fork F6
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 45A(1)-(3) the principal may appoint substitute attorneys, expressly in the instrument; (4) "A substitute attorney
-- may act as attorney under the power of attorney during a vacancy in the office of the specified attorney or a vacancy
-- of a kind specified in the instrument". s 20(4): under an enduring power the substitute must also have accepted.
@export Can my substitute attorney act for me now (ss 5, 20(4), 45A)?
GIVEN `I appointed the substitute expressly in my document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney document expressly appoints this person as substitute for a named attorney
      `what has happened to my attorney` IS A `What has happened to my attorney` @desc What has happened to the attorney the substitute replaces. One of: "my appointment of them was revoked", "they renounced the power", "they died", "they became bankrupt", "they are a corporation that was dissolved", "they lost the capacity to continue to act as attorney", "a circumstance the regulations prescribe", "none of these"
      `a vacancy of a kind my document specifies has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a vacancy of a kind your document itself names (for example the attorney being overseas) has occurred
      `my power is an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is an enduring one (see the s 19 question)
      `the substitute has signed to accept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the substitute has signed the document to accept the appointment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my substitute attorney act for me now` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I appointed the substitute expressly in my document`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 45A(2) "may be made by"; other ways of appointing are not addressed)
           IF     (NOT `there is a vacancy in the office of` `what has happened to my attorney`)
              AND (NOT `a vacancy of a kind my document specifies has occurred`)
           THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 45A(4) "during a vacancy": a period the text fixes
           IF `my power is an enduring power of attorney` AND (NOT `the substitute has signed to accept`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 20(1), (4)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 46 -- when one of several attorneys' offices falls vacant`

-- s 46(1) "If a power of attorney appoints 2 or more persons as joint attorneys, the power of attorney is terminated if
-- the office of one or more of the attorneys becomes vacant." (1A) "However, such a power of attorney is not terminated
-- if (a) the power of attorney provides otherwise, and (b) at least one of the attorneys or a substitute attorney remains
-- in office." (2) appointed severally or jointly and severally: "a vacancy ... does not operate to terminate the power of
-- attorney in relation to the other attorneys". Schedule 5 cl 10: the 2013 amendment of s 46 does not apply to a power
-- created before it; the earlier s 46 is not deposited.
@export Does my power of attorney end because one of my attorneys' offices has fallen vacant (ss 5, 46)?
GIVEN `how my attorneys were appointed` IS A `How my attorneys were appointed` @desc How your document appoints your attorneys. One of: "jointly" (they must act together), "severally" (each may act alone), "jointly and severally" (together or alone), "I appointed only one attorney"
      `what has happened to one of my attorneys` IS A `What has happened to my attorney` @desc What has happened to one of your attorneys. One of: "my appointment of them was revoked", "they renounced the power", "they died", "they became bankrupt", "they are a corporation that was dissolved", "they lost the capacity to continue to act as attorney", "a circumstance the regulations prescribe", "none of these"
      `my document provides that it continues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document says the power continues if a joint attorney's office falls vacant
      `at least one attorney or substitute remains in office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one of your attorneys, or a substitute attorney, remains in office
      `my document was signed before the 2013 amendments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your document was signed before the Powers of Attorney Amendment Act 2013 amended s 46
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a vacancy end my power of attorney` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is a vacancy in the office of` `what has happened to one of my attorneys`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 46(1) "if the office ... becomes vacant"
    ELSE CONSIDER `how my attorneys were appointed`
         WHEN `jointly` THEN
             BRANCH IF `my document was signed before the 2013 amendments` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (Sch 5 cl 10 points to the earlier s 46, not deposited)
                    IF `my document provides that it continues` AND `at least one attorney or substitute remains in office` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 46(1A)
                    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 46(1)
         WHEN `severally` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 46(2), a flat "does not operate to terminate"
         WHEN `jointly and severally` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 46(2)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 46 is silent on a sole attorney; the general law decides)

§§ `s 50 -- my estate under management`

-- s 50(1) a power "is not terminated by the estate of the principal becoming subject to management under the NSW Trustee
-- and Guardian Act 2009"; (3) "A power of attorney is suspended while the estate of the principal is a managed estate";
-- (4), (5) NCAT may order the power to remain in force for the part of the estate excluded from (or not under) its
-- financial management order; (7) the Supreme Court may restore it; (13) not a power given before Schedule 1 to the
-- Conveyancing (Powers of Attorney) Amendment Act 1983 commenced; (14) subject to Part 3 (irrevocable powers).
@export Is my power of attorney suspended, for this part of my affairs, because my estate is under financial management (s 50)?
GIVEN `my estate is under management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your estate is under management under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 (for example by a financial management order)
      `the tribunal ordered my power to stay in force for this part of my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT, when making the financial management order, ordered your power of attorney to stay in force for the part of your estate this question is about
      `the Supreme Court restored my power for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has restored your power of attorney to operation to the extent this question is about
      `my power is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is irrevocable (see the s 15 question)
      `my power was given before the 1983 amendments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power was given before Schedule 1 to the Conveyancing (Powers of Attorney) Amendment Act 1983 commenced
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my power suspended because my estate is managed` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my power was given before the 1983 amendments` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 50(13): the section does not apply; the text is silent on what does)
           IF `my power is irrevocable` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 50(14) "subject to Part 3", which does not speak of managed estates; fork F7)
           IF (NOT `my estate is under management`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 50(3) "while": a period the text fixes
           IF `the tribunal ordered my power to stay in force for this part of my estate` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 50(4), (5)
           IF `the Supreme Court restored my power for this` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 50(7)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 50(3)

§§ `ss 47-49 -- acts after the power ended or was suspended`

-- s 47 an attorney who acts within the scope of a terminated or suspended power "without knowing of the termination or
-- suspension is entitled to rely on the power"; s 48(2) no reliance for an act done "with notice of the termination or
-- suspension".
@export Can my attorney rely on my power for an act done after it ended or was suspended (ss 47, 48(2))?
GIVEN `the act was within the scope of the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act would have been within what the power allowed, had it not ended or been suspended
      `my attorney knew it had ended or been suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney knew, or had notice, when acting that the power had ended or been suspended
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my attorney rely on the power after it ended` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my attorney knew it had ended or been suspended` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 48(2) "does not entitle"
           IF `the act was within the scope of the power` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 47
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 47 limits the grant in its own words; outside it the text is silent)

-- s 48(1) "a third party who deals or otherwise transacts in good faith with the attorney without knowing of the
-- termination or suspension is entitled to rely on the power of attorney".
@export Can someone who dealt with my attorney after my power ended or was suspended rely on the power (s 48(1))?
GIVEN `they dealt in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person dealt with your attorney in good faith
      `they knew it had ended or been suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person knew the power had ended or been suspended
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a person who dealt with my attorney rely on the power` MEANS
    IF `they dealt in good faith` AND (NOT `they knew it had ended or been suspended`)
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 48(1)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 48(1) limits the grant in its own words; outside it the general law decides)

-- s 49(1) "An attorney under a power of attorney that is terminated must not do any act or thing under the power of
-- attorney if the attorney knows of the termination at the time"; (2) the same for a suspended authority. "Maximum
-- penalty--5 years imprisonment." s 54(1): prosecuted on indictment. Written as a prohibition on the attorney, run from
-- the time the power ends (time 0); the attorney's knowing act, if any, is the event at time 0.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Attorney party` `Attorney act`
`s 49 -- the attorney must not act under the power knowing it has ended or been suspended` MEANS
    PARTY `the attorney`
    SHANT `do an act under the power knowing it has ended or been suspended`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the attorney` BECAUSE "the attorney did an act under the power knowing it had been terminated or the authority suspended (s 49)"

@export Has my attorney committed the offence of acting under my power of attorney knowing it had ended or been suspended (s 49)?
GIVEN `my power had ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney had been terminated when your attorney acted
      `my attorney's authority for the act had been suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney's authority to do that act had been suspended (for example while your estate was under management)
      `my attorney acted under the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney did an act or thing under the power after that
      `my attorney knew at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney knew, at the time of the act, of the termination or suspension
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Has my attorney committed the s 49 offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my power had ended`) AND (NOT `my attorney's authority for the act had been suspended`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 49 "that is terminated", "where the authority ... has been suspended"
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 49 -- the attorney must not act under the power knowing it has ended or been suspended` 0 `the events`
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `my attorney acted under the power` AND `my attorney knew at the time`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the attorney` `do an act under the power knowing it has ended or been suspended` 0)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 2)

@export What is the most my attorney can be imprisoned for, in years, for acting under my ended or suspended power (ss 49, 54); 0 if s 49 is not broken on these facts?
GIVEN `my power had ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney had been terminated when your attorney acted
      `my attorney's authority for the act had been suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney's authority to do that act had been suspended
      `my attorney acted under the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney did an act or thing under the power after that
      `my attorney knew at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney knew, at the time of the act, of the termination or suspension
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most my attorney can be imprisoned for under s 49` MEANS
    IF `Has my attorney committed the s 49 offence` `my power had ended` `my attorney's authority for the act had been suspended` `my attorney acted under the power` `my attorney knew at the time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN 5
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 36(5) -- revoking my enduring power`

-- s 36(5) "An enduring power of attorney can not be lawfully revoked by the principal while the principal is declared to
-- be incapable by such an order." How a power is otherwise revoked is the general law (s 7).
@export Can I lawfully revoke my enduring power of attorney now (s 36(5))?
GIVEN `my power is an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is an enduring one (see the s 19 question)
      `a tribunal order declares me incapable now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NCAT or the Supreme Court has made an order under s 36(5) declaring that you lack capacity because of mental incapacity, covering the present time
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I revoke my enduring power now` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `my power is an enduring power of attorney`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 36(5) speaks only of enduring powers)
           IF `a tribunal order declares me incapable now` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 36(5), a flat "can not be lawfully revoked"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the Act is silent on how to revoke; the general law decides, s 7)

§§ `ss 26, 27, 33, 35 -- applying for a review`

-- s 35(1) "Each of the following persons is an interested person": (a) an attorney (including one whose appointment has
-- been purportedly revoked), (b) the principal, (c) a guardian or enduring guardian of the principal, (d) "any other
-- person who, in the opinion of the review tribunal, has a proper interest in the proceedings or a genuine concern for
-- the welfare of the principal". s 36(1) the tribunal may review "on the application of an interested person".
-- s 33(2) NCAT and the Supreme Court have jurisdiction over an enduring power (including its revocation); (3) only the
-- Supreme Court over any other power "given by a principal who is incommunicate for the time being". s 6(6)(a): a
-- protected power under the old Conveyancing Act counts as enduring. s 27(2) a person "cannot" apply for the same
-- function in respect of the same matter if already applied to the other tribunal, (3) unless that application was
-- withdrawn with the tribunal's approval. Shared by both seats.
GIVEN `my place` IS A `My place in relation to the power`
      `the tribunal finds I have a proper interest or genuine concern` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal` IS A `The review tribunal`
      `the power is enduring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal is incommunicate now` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I already applied to the other tribunal about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that application was withdrawn with approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may apply for a review` `my place` `the tribunal finds I have a proper interest or genuine concern` `the tribunal` `the power is enduring` `the principal is incommunicate now` `I already applied to the other tribunal about the same matter` `that application was withdrawn with approval` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `an interested person`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 35(1), fork F8
           IF (NOT `the tribunal has jurisdiction`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 33(1) "if ... as provided by this section"
           IF `I already applied to the other tribunal about the same matter` AND (NOT `that application was withdrawn with approval`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 27(2) "cannot", (3)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `an interested person` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my place`
            WHEN `someone else, such as a relative or friend` THEN `the tribunal finds I have a proper interest or genuine concern`
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the tribunal has jurisdiction` MEANS
               `the power is enduring`
            OR (    `the principal is incommunicate now`
                AND `the tribunal` EQUALS `the Supreme Court`)

@export Can I, the principal, apply to NCAT or the Supreme Court for a review of my power of attorney (ss 4, 27, 33, 35, 36)?
GIVEN `the tribunal I would apply to` IS A `The review tribunal` @desc Where you would apply. One of: "the Civil and Administrative Tribunal" (NCAT), "the Supreme Court"
      `my power is an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power of attorney is an enduring one (see the s 19 question), or an older "protected" power under the Conveyancing Act 1919
      `an incapacity makes me unable to understand communications about my property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physical or mental incapacity (temporary or permanent, including one caused by a drug or treatment) makes you unable to understand communications about your property or affairs
      `an incapacity makes me unable to express my intentions about my property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such an incapacity makes you unable to express your intentions about your property or affairs
      `I cannot be located or contacted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot be located or contacted (an application may be carried on for you, s 42)
      `I already applied to the other tribunal about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already applied to the other review tribunal for the same thing about the same (or substantially the same) matter
      `that application was withdrawn with approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that earlier application was withdrawn with that tribunal's approval
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for a review of my power of attorney` MEANS
    `may apply for a review` `I am the principal` FALSE `the tribunal I would apply to` `my power is an enduring power of attorney` (`the principal is incommunicate` `an incapacity makes me unable to understand communications about my property or affairs` `an incapacity makes me unable to express my intentions about my property or affairs` `I cannot be located or contacted`) `I already applied to the other tribunal about the same matter` `that application was withdrawn with approval`

§§ `s 25 -- an enduring power made in another State or Territory`

-- s 25(1) "An interstate enduring power of attorney has effect in this State as if it were an enduring power of attorney
-- made under, and in compliance with, this Act, but only to the extent that the powers it gives under the law of the
-- State or Territory in which it was made could validly have been given by an enduring power of attorney made under this
-- Act." (3) not a power the regulations prescribe. (5) "interstate enduring power of attorney (a) means a power of
-- attorney made by instrument in another State or Territory that, under the law of the State or Territory, has effect
-- ... as a valid power of attorney even if the principal loses capacity ..., and (b) includes an instrument in the nature
-- of an enduring power of attorney, however described."
@export Does my enduring power of attorney made in another Australian State or Territory work in NSW for this power (s 25)?
GIVEN `I made it in another State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the power of attorney in an Australian State or Territory other than NSW
      `it stays valid there if I lose capacity, or is of that nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under that State's or Territory's law, it stays valid even if you lose mental capacity, or it is otherwise in the nature of an enduring power of attorney however it is described
      `the regulations exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether NSW regulations prescribe this power (or its class) as excluded from s 25
      `a NSW enduring power could validly give this power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power you are asking about could validly have been given by an enduring power of attorney made under the NSW Act
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my interstate enduring power work in NSW` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I made it in another State or Territory`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25 is not about NSW powers; use the s 19 question)
           IF (NOT `it stays valid there if I lose capacity, or is of that nature`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 25(5) "includes": the definition is not closed)
           IF `the regulations exclude it` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 25(3) "does not apply"
           IF `a NSW enduring power could validly give this power` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 25(1)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 25(1) "but only to the extent"

§§ `s 44 -- a certified copy of my power`

-- s 44(1) "A document is a certified copy of an instrument for the purposes of this section if (a) there is endorsed on
-- the document a written certificate, to the effect that the document is a true and complete copy ..., by (i) the
-- principal ..., or (ii) a person (or person belonging to a class of persons) prescribed by the regulations ..., and
-- (b) each page of the document bears the signature of the person who gives the certificate". (2) it is then evidence
-- against the principal of execution and contents. (5) a knowingly false certificate: maximum penalty 5 years.
@export Is this copy of my power of attorney a certified copy that can be used as evidence (s 44)?
GIVEN `who certified the copy` IS A `Who certified the copy` @desc Who wrote the certificate on the copy. One of: "I did, as the principal", "a person of the class the regulations prescribe" (for example, under the transitional rule, the classes in the old Conveyancing (General) Regulation 2003 cl 49), "another person"
      `the certificate says it is a true and complete copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate is written on the copy and says it is a true and complete copy of the original document
      `every page is signed by the certifier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each page of the copy bears the certifier's signature
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this a certified copy of my power of attorney` MEANS
    IF     `a permitted certifier`
       AND `the certificate says it is a true and complete copy`
       AND `every page is signed by the certifier`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 44(1) "if" (a) and (b)
    WHERE
        `a permitted certifier` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who certified the copy`
            WHEN `another person` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 52 -- deeds affecting my land`

-- s 52(1) "A conveyance or other deed affecting land executed on or after 1 July 1920 under a power of attorney has no
-- effect unless the instrument creating the power has been registered." (2) registration later has effect as if before;
-- (4) "This section does not apply to a lease for a term of 3 years or less."
@export Is a deed affecting my land that my attorney signed without effect because my power of attorney is not registered (s 52)?
GIVEN `the day my attorney signed the deed` IS A DATE @desc The day your attorney signed the conveyance or other deed affecting your land
      `the deed is a lease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deed is a lease
      `the lease term in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is a lease, its term in months (any number if it is not a lease)
      `my power of attorney is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document creating your power of attorney has been registered in the General Register of Deeds (registration after the deed was signed counts)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my attorney's deed affecting my land without effect for want of registration` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day my attorney signed the deed` `is before` (`the date` 1 7 1920) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 52(1) "on or after 1 July 1920"
           IF `the deed is a lease` AND `the lease term in months` AT MOST 36 THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 52(4) "does not apply"
           IF `my power of attorney is registered` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 52(1), (2)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- s 52(1) "has no effect unless"
